Subject: CB-5 protection settings - NYSEG revised short-circuit data

NYSEG issued revised short-circuit data at Kintigh last week following two neighbouring
large-load energizations. Our engineer of record has to re-run the CB-5 coordination and
arc-flash studies against the new fault levels and resubmit the settings package. We expect
the re-study to take 3 to 5 weeks. NYSEG has told us to expect 4 to 6 weeks of review after
resubmittal. We will update the delivery forecast once we have the resubmittal date.
